<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan's Lever Bros rises 4.7 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan's Lever Bros rises 4.7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lever Brothers Pakistan Ltd 50-rupee stock rose 35 rupees, or 4.7 percent, to 780 on Friday after completion of its recent merger with Brooke Bond Pakistan Ltd, dealers said.</p>
<p>Some 200 shares had changed hands at the Karachi Stock Exchange by 11:37 a.m. (0637 GMT), one dealer said.</p>
<p>Lever Brothers manufactures consumer items, including edible oils, ice cream, soaps and detergents. It paid a 100 percent cash dividend for the 18 months ended June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
